test_hextotet -- the commands hextotet and grid2grid (Oct 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_hextotet_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     9 decks, under 1 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  hextotet / N / mo_sink / mo_source splits every cell of the source
  mesh; grid2grid / name / mo_sink / mo_source is the same command with
  readable option names (it calls hextotet). The options:

     2  quad    -> 2 triangles                       quadtotri2
     4  quad    -> 4 triangles, + the quad centre     quadtotri4
     4  pyramid -> 4 tets, + the base centre          pyrtotet4
     3  prism   -> 3 tets                             prismtotet3
     5  hex     -> 5 tets                             hextotet5
     6  hex     -> 6 tets                             hextotet6
    14  prism   -> 14 tets, + centroid, 3 quad face centres
                                                      prismtotet14
    18  prism   -> 18 tets, + centroid, 5 face centres prismtotet18
    24  hex     -> 24 tets, + centroid, 6 face centres hextotet24
  (no N)   the mesh type decides: hex 6, prism 3, quad 2, pyramid 4

THE DECKS

  ht01_hex_brick     the hex part of the deck in issue #214: a 2x2x2
                     createpts brick to 5, 6, 24
  ht02_hex_2mat      2x2x2 hexes, two materials, vertex field f: 5, 6,
                     24 by hextotet and by grid2grid (same files)
  ht03_hex_jitter    3x3x3 hexes, interior vertices moved (warped inner
                     faces, flat outside): 5, 6, 24 must still conform
  ht04_prism_2mat    16 prisms, both diagonals, two materials, f: 3,
                     14, 18 by hextotet and grid2grid
  ht05_prism_stack   the prism part of issue #214 (stack / fill), in
                     its order 3, 18, 14
  ht06_quad          3x2 quads: 2 and 4, hextotet and grid2grid
  ht07_pyramid       the unit cube as 6 pyramids: 4, both commands
  ht08_defaults      no option, on hex, prism, quad and pyramid meshes
  ht09_refused       options that do not fit the cells (3, 14, 18 on
                     hexes; 24, 5 on prisms; an unknown grid2grid name):
                     refused with a message, LaGriT carries on, and a
                     valid split after them still works

  Header lines at the top of each deck say what to check:
    # split   : OUT.inp SRC.inp N   OUT must be SRC split by option N
    # same    : A.inp B.inp         the two files must be identical
    # refused : TEXT                TEXT must be in the deck's output
  The sources are made by make_hextotet_inputs.py (fixed seed) or by
  the deck itself (ht01, ht05 dump theirs).

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_hextotet.py; definitions in its opening comment)

  Every deck: LaGriT finished; no MMVERIFY message, no signal, no
  FATAL. Every split, against answers computed from the source alone:
  cell type and count; vertex count, the source vertices unchanged and
  first, every new vertex at a distinct centroid or face centre (a
  face shared by two cells gets one) and none missing; every cell with
  positive volume, the total = the source volume; a conforming split
  (no face in more than two cells, and the outside area = the source's
  outside area, so no gaps or overlaps); every cell inside exactly one
  source cell with its material, and filling it; the linear field
  f = 1 + 2x + 3y + 5z exact at every vertex. Measured, not judged:
  smallest and largest dihedral angle (triangles: angle), imt of the
  new vertices.

  summary.html shows each source and result coloured by material, and
  the cells made from one source cell, exploded (shrunk and pushed
  apart) so each can be seen.

FIXED WITH THIS SUITE (src/hextotet_hybrid.f, src/hextotet_check_types.f)

  #214  prism to 14 tets wrote past its work arrays (ilist sized for
        5 vertices, not the prism's 6; the face slots indexed by face
        number 3-5 instead of 1-3): heap damage, abort. Sometimes the
        damage only showed in a later command (3 then 18 aborted).
  -     every option that adds vertices read the source vertex arrays
        past their end (valgrind; harmless so far).
  -     pyramid to 4 tets was the 14/18 prism code: 8 tets and 2 new
        vertices per pyramid, written into arrays sized for 4 and 1
        (MMVERIFY PANIC, abort). Now as documented: 4 tets, one new
        vertex at the base centre.
  -     an option that does not fit the cells (14 on hexes: memory
        corruption, abort; 3 on hexes: meaningless "tets") is refused
        before anything is made.
  -     no option on a quad mesh gave 24 (tets from quads, with an
        interpolation error); the documented default is 2.
  On LaGriT without these fixes ht04, ht05, ht07, ht08 and ht09 fail.

FILES

  run_hextotet_tests.sh    runner (work/, logs/; WORK= and LOGS= may
                           change them)
  make_hextotet_inputs.py  the source meshes
  check_hextotet.py        checks, summary.html (pictures with
                           ../test_lagrit_upstream/draw_meshes.py)
  ht01-ht09 *.lgi          the decks
